{"strongs": "H3595", "word": "כִּיֹּר", "translit": "kiy.yor", "root": "כיר", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun masculine", "gloss": "pot, basin", "definition": "כִּיֹּר , כִּיּוֺר noun masculine 1Kgs 7:38 pot, basin (Late Hebrew כִּיּוֺר wash-basin , so Aramaic כִּיּוֺרָא ) — absolute כִּיֹּר 1Kgs 7:30 + 8 t.; כִּיּוֺר 1Sam 2:14 + 5 t.; construct כִּיּוֺר Exod 30:18 + 2 t.; plural absolute כִּיֹּרוֺת 1Kgs 7:40 (but see below), 2Chr 4:14 כְּיֹּרֹת 1Kgs 7:43 כִּיּוֺרִים 2Chr 4:6 construct כְּיֹּרוֺת 1Kgs 7:38 — 1. pot for cooking 1Sam 2:14 (|| דּוּד , קַלַּחַת , פָּרוּר ). 2. fire-pot כִּיּוֺר אֵשׁ Zech 12:6 (|| לַפִּיד אֵשׁ ; figurative of chiefs of Judah). 3. basin of bronze for washing, laver ; set on a bronze support \\ \\ a. before tabernacle Exod 30:18 ; Exod 30:28 ; Exod 31:9 ; Exod 35:16 ; Exod 38:8 ; Exod 39:39 ; Exod 40:7 ; Exod 40:11 ; Exod 40:30 ; Lev 8:11 (all P ). \\ \\ b. 10 in number, 5 at each front corner of temple 1Kgs 7:30 ; 1Kgs 7:38 (3 t. in verse); 1Kgs 7:43 = 2Chr 4:14 ; 2Chr 4:6 ( 1Kgs 7:40 read הַסִּירוֺת as v 1Kgs 7:45 and || 2Chr 4:11 ; 2Chr 4:16 , so Hebrew Manuscripts ᵐ5 ᵑ9 Th Ke Sta Klo and others) 4. plat form or stage of bronze (probably round, bowl-like in shape) on which, according to Chronicles, Solomon stood and kneeled 2Chr 6:13 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3963')\">BDB3963</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3595')\">H3595</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3962')\">BDB3962</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB3964')\">BDB3964</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>כִּיֹּר</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>כִּיּוֺר</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"1Kgs 7:38\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(11,7,38)\">1Kgs 7:38</ref></sup> <highlightword>pot, basin</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <bdbheb>כִּיּוֺר</bdbheb> <highlight>wash-basin</highlight>, so Aramaic <bdbarc>כִּיּוֺרָא</bdbarc>) — absolute <bdbheb>כִּיֹּר</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 7:30\" b=\"1